I am in the flat.
I look at my calendar.
I write Anitha's name in the calendar.
Coffee is on Thursday evening at five-thirty.
Then I see a problem.
I have a haircut on Thursday evening at five-thirty!
I quickly take my phone.
I call the beauty parlor again.
The woman at the parlor answers the phone.
"Hello," she says.
"Sorry, I have another thing on Thursday," I say.
"Can I come on Friday?" I ask.
"You can come, what time will you come on Friday?" she asks.
"Can I come at six forty-five in the evening?" I ask.
"Okay, come on Friday evening at six forty-five," she says.
"Thank you very much," I say.
I write the new time in the calendar.
Now I have an event every day.
Therefore I always look at my calendar.
